            "subheading": "Step 1",
            "title": "Sourcing the leathers and materials",
            "heading_font_size": "heading-large",
            "text": "<p>The leathers and materials used to make our shoes are sourced from all over the world. The most common source of leather is from bovine animals such as calves and cows. These animal skins are used for both the soles and uppers of our shoes.</p><p>We offer a wide range of options when it comes to the leathers and materials used for our shoes. We have over 50 different options available in terms of colours, textures and finishes. We source our leathers and materials from the best tanneries and suppliers in the world to ensure that our products are of the highest quality.</p><p>Once you've designed and ordered your perfect pair of bespoke shoes, the process begin with gathering different materials in our workshop according to specifications for customizations.</p>",
