          "type": "timeline",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Step 3",
            "title": "Sewing and sole mounting",
            "heading_font_size": "heading-large",
            "text": "<p>Once the leather was stretched and cleaned, they skillfully lined up their sewing machines in rhythm between the lining and the upper, the front support (puff) and the back support (counter) were inserted. The shoe upper is then fitted around the last using lost-head nails, distributed along the perimeter of the foot. Once all the different elements (meaning the sole, plant and pattern), they will be sewn into shape with great care to ensure that no part goes unnoticed or gets overlooked during this process</p><p>The best different construction techniques used in men’s footwear are Blake stitched and Goodyear stitching, they provide higher quality and offer unique benefits.</p><p>After the sewing was finished, it was time to move on to the next stage: sole mounting.</p><p>This is where the shoemaker attaches the sole to the upper part of the shoe. This is a critical step in the process, as it determines how comfortable the final product will be</p><p>Once the sole has been mounted, the shoemaker will check to make sure that everything is in order and that there are no defects. If everything looks good, the shoes will then be sent to the finishing department.<br/><br/></p>",
